==Polish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|pl|sla-pro|*byti}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|pl}} {{m|ine-pro|*bʰuh₂-}} (see Proto-Indo-European {{m|ine-pro|*bʰew-}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[bɨt͡ɕ]|lang=pl}}
* {{audio|pl-być.ogg|audio|lang=pl}}
* {{rhymes|lang=pl|ɨt͡ɕ}}

===Verb===
{{pl-verb|a=impf}}

# to [[be]] {{qualifier|indicates sameness or membership in a class}} {{+obj|pl|nom|or|ins}}
# to [[be]] {{qualifier|auxilary verb used for [[predication]]}} {{+obj|pl|adjective}}
#: {{ux|pl|'''Jestem''' zmęczona.|t=I '''am''' tired.}}
# {{non-gloss definition|In future tense, forms future tense of imperfective verbs.}} {{+obj|pl|infinitive|or|verb in past tense}}
# {{lb|pl|archaic}} {{non-gloss definition|In past tense, forms pluperfect tense.}} {{+obj|pl|verb in past tense}}
#* '''1869''', Charles Edmond (translated by Edmund Chojecki), ''Alkhadar: uste̜p z dziejów ojców naszych'', F.A. Brockhaus, page 231
#*: {{ux|pl|Nastusia na pół osunięta, na pół wsparta na dębie, na pół omdlała, z oczyma szeroko, nieruchomie otwartemi, utkwionemi w stronę, gdzie jastrząb dokonał '''był''' pomyślnych swoich łowów, strasznie dyszała.}}

====Usage notes====
The object is either in [[nominative]] or [[instrumental case]]; the former is often used when introducing oneself, and implies the object to be definite ({{m|pl|[[ja|Ja]] jestem [[Czesław]], [[a]] [[to]] jest [[Marysia]].}}), in the latter the object is usually indefinite ({{m|pl|Ona jest [[studentka|studentką]]}} = She is a student), although not exclusively ({{ux|pl|[[w|W]] [[ten|tym]] [[moment|momencie]] [[zorientować się|zorientował się]], [[że]] Bruce Wayne jest [[Batman]]em.|inline=1|t=In that moment he realised that Bruce Wayne is the Batman.}}.

